---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/legal-layout.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '@/lib/github-api';

const lastUpdated = 'November 3, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service - MoneyMatter"
  description="MoneyMatter Terms of Service - Read our terms and conditions for using the service."
  crossLinks={[{ href: '/privacy-policy', label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <h1 class="mb-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

  <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        By accessing or using MoneyMatter ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you
        do not agree to these terms, please do not use the Service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Description of Service</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        MoneyMatter is a personal finance management application that allows you to track expenses, manage budgets,
        connect bank accounts, and analyze your financial data. The Service is provided "as is" and "as available."
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-3">
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>Use the Service for any illegal purpose</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Service or its systems</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Service</li>
          <li>Upload malicious code or content</li>
          <li>Scrape or collect data from other users</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Bank Integrations</h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-3">
        <p>If you choose to connect your bank accounts, you acknowledge that:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>You are providing your own API credentials or authorizing access through OAuth</li>
          <li>We act as an intermediary and are not responsible for bank API availability</li>
          <li>Bank connections may require periodic re-authorization</li>
          <li>Transaction data accuracy depends on the information provided by your bank</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Data and Content</h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-3">
        <p>
          You retain ownership of all financial data you enter into the Service. By using the Service, you grant us
          a limited license to store, process, and display your data solely for the purpose of providing the
          Service.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the accuracy of the data you enter and for maintaining backups of important
          information.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. Open Source License</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        MoneyMatter is open source software licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0
        (AGPL-3.0). You may self-host, study, and modify the software in accordance with this license. If
        you run a modified version of MoneyMatter as a network service, you must publish your modifications
        under the same license. The source code is available on{' '}
        <a
          href={GITHUB_URL}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-primary hover:underline"
        >
          GitHub</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. Plans, Trial and Billing</h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-3">
        <p>
          Self-hosting MoneyMatter is free under the open source license above. Using our hosted service
          (moneymatter.app) requires a paid plan after a free trial.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Trial.</strong> New accounts get a 40-day trial with no payment method
          required. One trial per person; deleting and re-creating an account does not restart it. Backup restore
          is not available during the trial; backup export and data export are. When the trial ends without a
          subscription, your account becomes read-only: you can still sign in, view your data, export it and delete
          your account, but you cannot add or change data until you subscribe.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Plans and prices.</strong> Current plans, what each includes and their
          prices are listed on the pricing section of our website. Prices are shown without tax; the tax that applies
          in your country is added at checkout. In the iOS app, the App Store shows the price for your region before
          you confirm, and it may differ from our website. We may change prices with at least 30 days' notice; a
          change applies from your next renewal after the notice. App Store price changes also follow Apple's rules.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Merchant of record.</strong> Purchases on the web are processed by Stripe
          under Stripe Managed Payments. Stripe is the seller of record for your subscription: it collects payment and applicable
          taxes, issues receipts, and handles refunds, chargebacks and payment support. Your purchase is also subject
          to the terms Stripe shows you at checkout. Purchases in the iOS app are made through Apple In-App Purchase.
          Apple is the seller of record: it collects payment and applicable taxes, issues receipts, and handles refunds
          and payment support, and your purchase is also subject to{' '}
          <a
            href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary hover:underline">Apple's Media Services Terms</a
          >. We never see or store your card details.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Renewal and cancellation.</strong> Subscriptions renew automatically,
          monthly or yearly, until cancelled. You can cancel a web subscription at any time from Settings → Plan
          &amp; billing. After
          cancelling you keep access until the end of the period you have paid for, then your account becomes
          read-only. Switching plans is done from the same page; the charge or credit for a switch is shown before
          you confirm it. To cancel or switch a subscription bought in the iOS app, use your{' '}
          <a
            href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary hover:underline">App Store subscriptions</a
          >. Deleting your account does not cancel an App Store subscription.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Refunds.</strong> If you ask within 14 days of your first payment on the
          web, we refund it in full, no questions asked: email{' '}
          <a href="mailto:support@moneymatter.app" class="text-primary hover:underline">support@moneymatter.app</a>.
          Other refund requests for web purchases are handled by Stripe as merchant of record, under its refund policy,
          using the link in your receipt. We cannot refund App Store purchases; request those from Apple at{' '}
          <a
            href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary hover:underline">reportaproblem.apple.com</a
          >. A refunded payment ends the subscription it paid for.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Failed payments.</strong> If a web renewal payment fails, Stripe retries it and
          emails you to update your payment method. If every retry fails, the subscription is cancelled and your
          account becomes read-only. If an App Store renewal fails, Apple retries it, and your account can become
          read-only until the payment succeeds. Your data is not deleted.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Early Adopter plan.</strong> Accounts that were active before paid plans
          launched may be granted the Early Adopter plan free of charge. It includes the features that existed in the
          Essential and Plus plans on the launch date, for the lifetime of the Service, together with bug fixes and
          improvements to those features. Features added after the launch date, and features that cost us money per
          user to run, belong to the paid plans; Early Adopter accounts get 50% off any paid plan bought on the web for as
          long as they keep it. The grant is personal to the account, cannot be transferred or exchanged for money, and may be
          withdrawn for violation of these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Changes to features.</strong> We may add, change or remove features of a
          plan. If we remove a feature you are paying for, you may cancel and request a refund for the unused part of
          the current period through Stripe, or through Apple for an App Store subscription.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">8. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-3">
        <p>
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT
          THE SERVICE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR SECURE.
        </p>
        <p>
          MoneyMatter is not a financial advisor. The Service is for informational and tracking purposes only. You
          should consult a qualified financial professional for financial advice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
        CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOSS OF DATA OR FINANCIAL LOSSES, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE
        SERVICE.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">10. Service Modifications</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        We reserve the right to modify, suspend, or discontinue the Service at any time without notice. We are not
        liable for any modification, suspension, or discontinuation of the Service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">11. Termination</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        We may terminate or suspend your account at any time for violation of these terms. Non-payment does not
        delete your account; it becomes read-only as described in section 7. You may delete your
        account at any time through the application settings. Upon termination, your right to use the Service will
        immediately cease.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">12. Changes to Terms</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        We may update these Terms of Service from time to time. Continued use of the Service after changes
        constitutes acceptance of the new terms. We will notify users of significant changes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">13. Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
        For questions about these Terms, please open an issue on our{' '}
        <a
          href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-primary hover:underline"
        >
          GitHub repository</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
